{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftStats","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" supports complete inferential statistics with numerical stability across extreme sample offsets, large degrees of freedom ("},{"code":"df >= 2e5","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" via Temme uniform asymptotic expansion), and sub-machine-epsilon upper tails."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"1. Two-Sample Welch \/ Student t-Test","level":3,"anchor":"1-Two-Sample-Welch--Student-t-Test"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftStats","","let groupA: [Double] = [12.1, 14.3, 11.8, 13.5, 15.0]","let groupB: [Double] = [9.8, 10.5, 11.2, 10.1, 9.4]","","let result = try Stats.tTest(sample1: groupA, sample2: groupB)","print(\"t-statistic: \\(result.statistic), p-value: \\(result.pValue)\")","if result.isSignificant {","    print(\"Statistically significant difference (p < 0.05)\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"2. One-Way ANOVA","level":3,"anchor":"2-One-Way-ANOVA"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let samples: [[Double]] = [groupA, groupB, [8.5, 9.0, 8.8]]","let anova = try Stats.oneWayANOVA(groups: samples)","print(\"F-statistic: \\(anova.fStatistic), p-value: \\(anova.pValue)\")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"3. Chi-Square Goodness-of-Fit","level":3,"anchor":"3-Chi-Square-Goodness-of-Fit"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Stats.chiSquareGoodnessOfFit(observed:expected:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" requires at least two categories, finite non-negative observed frequencies, and strictly positive finite expected frequencies. Upper-tail survival probabilities use direct Lentz continued fractions and Temme asymptotics ("},{"code":"a = df \/ 2 >= 1e5","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let chi2 = try Stats.chiSquareGoodnessOfFit(","    observed: [20, 30, 50],","    expected: [25, 25, 50]",")","print(\"chi2 = \\(chi2.statistic), p = \\(chi2.pValue), df = \\(chi2.degreesOfFreedom)\")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"4. Normality Tests (Shapiro–Wilk & Lilliefors KS)","level":3,"anchor":"4-Normality-Tests-Shapiro-Wilk--Lilliefors-KS"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Stats.shapiroWilk(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" implements Royston AS R94 for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"3 <= n <= 5000"},{"type":"text","text":" with shift\/scale invariance ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1e12"},{"type":"text","text":" offsets, subnormal to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1e308"},{"type":"text","text":" dynamic range) and rejects non-finite or constant samples."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Stats.kolmogorovSmirnov(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" implements the Lilliefors normality test against sample-fitted normal parameters ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n >= 5"},{"type":"text","text":") using Dallal–Wilkinson and Stephens calibrated p-values."}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let sample: [Double] = [2.1, 2.5, 2.7, 3.0, 3.1, 3.3, 3.8]","let sw = try Stats.shapiroWilk(sample)","let ks = try Stats.kolmogorovSmirnov(sample)","print(\"Shapiro-Wilk W = \\(sw.statistic), p = \\(sw.pValue)\")","print(\"Lilliefors D = \\(ks.statistic), p = \\(ks.pValue)\")"],"syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftStats\/documentation\/SwiftStats\/HypothesisTesting","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftStats\/documentation\/SwiftStats"]]},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Perform Student’s\/Welch’s t-tests, paired t-tests, Chi-Square goodness-of-fit tests, normality tests, and one-way ANOVA."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftstats\/hypothesistesting"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftStats\/documentation\/SwiftStats\/DescriptiveStatistics","doc:\/\/SwiftStats\/documentation\/SwiftStats\/ChoosingDotProductAccuracy","doc:\/\/SwiftStats\/documentation\/SwiftStats\/DecimalANOVA"],"title":"Guides & Tutorials","anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","generated":true}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SwiftStats"}],"title":"Hypothesis Testing & ANOVA","roleHeading":"Article"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://SwiftStats/documentation/SwiftStats":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftStats\/documentation\/SwiftStats","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vectorized Statistical Computing & Inferential Analytics."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftstats","title":"SwiftStats","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftStats/documentation/SwiftStats/DecimalANOVA":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftstats\/decimalanova","title":"ANOVA from original decimal observations","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftStats\/documentation\/SwiftStats\/DecimalANOVA","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Preserve small differences around a large offset before converting observations to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftStats/documentation/SwiftStats/ChoosingDotProductAccuracy":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Select the reduction policy for each operation. Both policies accept "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Double]"},{"type":"text","text":" inputs and return a "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftStats\/documentation\/SwiftStats\/ChoosingDotProductAccuracy","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Choosing dot-product accuracy","url":"\/documentation\/swiftstats\/choosingdotproductaccuracy"},"doc://SwiftStats/documentation/SwiftStats/DescriptiveStatistics":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Compute descriptive metrics, covariance, Pearson\/Spearman correlations, and matrix operations using Apple Accelerate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vDSP"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BLAS"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftstats\/descriptivestatistics","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftStats\/documentation\/SwiftStats\/DescriptiveStatistics","title":"Vectorized Descriptive Statistics & Linear Algebra"}}}